// Soundness cross-check of the points-to alias answers: the alias test pass,
// with use-points-to=1, asserts on every pair of `test.ptr` values that
// CIRBasicAliasAnalysis and the points-to analysis never give two different
// answers that are both not MayAlias (in particular never NoAlias against
// MustAlias). Run it over every points-to test, open and closed-tu; the
// alias-analysis*.cir tests in the parent directory run it in their own RUN
// lines. A failure is an assertion in the pass, so only the exit status is
// checked. When adding a points-to test, add it here.
//
// RUN: cir-opt %S/aggregate-values.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis=use-points-to=1 -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/aggregate-values.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis='use-points-to=1 closed-tu=1' -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/alias-basic.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis=use-points-to=1 -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/alias-basic.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis='use-points-to=1 closed-tu=1' -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/alias-escape.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis=use-points-to=1 -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/alias-escape.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis='use-points-to=1 closed-tu=1' -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/alias-ipo.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis=use-points-to=1 -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/alias-ipo.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis='use-points-to=1 closed-tu=1' -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
// RUN: cir-opt %S/array-cap.cir -test-cir-alias-analysis=use-points-to=1 -o /dev/null 2>/dev/null
